From: Eglantine PS5 <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 01:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Vulkan: command list copies can skip the fence window (off by default)

Core patch. Paths are the submodule's. Applies on core16 alone or in the lichii-cpu order.

Source: zortos293/Lichii PR 161, commit 3985ac21c6, GPL-3.0-or-later. PR 161 was still open on 6 Nov.

EDEN_NX2_LIST_COPY_FLUSH=1: SubmitNx2ListCopies flushes at once instead of asking DeferFlush.
ReadGpuWrittenCommands waits for these copies. Without this the front does not wait out the window:
WaitSubmittedTick asks the back through the idle hook, and the back flushes after its current ring
entry. So this is not needed for a longer window, it only removes that step, which matters when the
entry is long (a shader translation). Goes with:

    EDEN_NX2_FENCE_FLUSH_US=5000
    EDEN_NX2_LIST_COPY_FLUSH=1

The window switch and EDEN_NX2_FLUSH_DRAWS already exist in core16; PR 161's 5000 and 4096 are
defaults there and only env.txt lines here.

Pool memory: none itself. A longer window holds staging memory for a few ms more.

Checked: PS5-target syntax compile of the derived vulkan_rasterizer.cpp, 0 errors. Not run.

diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_rasterizer.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_rasterizer.cpp
index d14a7268ff..b0785e4134 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_rasterizer.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_rasterizer.cpp
@@ -1462,7 +1462,15 @@ void Vulkan::RasterizerVulkan::DisableGraphicsUniformBuffer(size_t stage, u32 in
 void RasterizerVulkan::FlushAll() {}
 
 void RasterizerVulkan::SubmitNx2ListCopies() {
-    if (buffer_cache.Nx2CopyListPages(scheduler.CurrentTick()) && !scheduler.DeferFlush()) {
+    // EDEN_NX2_LIST_COPY_FLUSH=1: command list copies go at once, whatever the fence window
+    // (EDEN_NX2_FENCE_FLUSH_US). Deferred, the front must ask the back for them (idle hook), and
+    // the back answers after its current ring entry. Lichii PR 161, commit 3985ac21c6.
+    static const bool at_once = [] {
+        const char* value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_LIST_COPY_FLUSH");
+        return value != nullptr && value[0] == '1';
+    }();
+    if (buffer_cache.Nx2CopyListPages(scheduler.CurrentTick()) &&
+        (at_once || !scheduler.DeferFlush())) {
         scheduler.Flush();
     }
 }
